// Dog Nobbler: the leaded marabou lure for reservoir trout credited to Trevor Housby, a painted split shot behind the eye.

id dog-nobbler
name "Dog Nobbler"
aliases "Nobbler"
type streamer
imitates baitfish attractor
naturals fry-minnow
difficulty beginner
species trout
season march april may june september october november
origin originator="Trevor Housby" region="England"
description "A painted split shot with an eye on each side crimped behind the hook's eye, a long black marabou tail with pearl flash and a black chenille body ribbed with silver wire."
history """
    Trevor Housby, a British all-round angler, made it for the big stocked rainbows of the
    reservoirs. Michael Jensen writes that it was in the 1970s, inspired by the small jigs
    American spin anglers used on ultralight tackle. Barry Ord Clarke credits Sid Knight, a
    professional tyer of Bridgnorth, instead. Keith Elliott's obituary of Fred J. Taylor says Taylor too
    played a key role in inventing it. The classic head is a coarse split shot crimped on and
    glued, painted with a yellow eye and a black pupil each side; beads, cones and dumbbell eyes
    are modern stand-ins.
    """
fishing """
    A stillwater lure for stocked rainbows, best early in the season. On a floating line and
    long leader, or a sinking line, make slow pulls with pauses: on every pause the leaded head
    dives and the marabou rises, so it jigs through the water. Cast it with an open loop: the
    shot makes it heavy.
    """
sources {
    "Global FlyFisher: Dog Nobbler heads (Michael Jensen)" url="https://globalflyfisher.com/node/71163"
    "Global FlyFisher: Caramel Tiger Dog Nobbler (Michael Jensen)" url="https://globalflyfisher.com/node/71316"
    "Global FlyFisher: Nobbler fly tying tutorial (Ívar's Fly Workshop)" url="https://globalflyfisher.com/video/nobbler-fly-tying-tutorial-ivars-fly-workshop"
    "Sexyloops: Dog Nobbler" url="https://www.sexyloops.com/glossary/dognobbler.shtml"
    "Fish4Flies: Palmered Eyed Dog Nobbler" url="https://www.fish4flies.com/Lures/Nobblers-and-Leadheads/Palmered-Eyed-Dog-Nobbler-Black"
    "Caught by the River: Caught by the Reaper, Fred J. Taylor (Keith Elliott)" url="https://www.caughtbytheriver.net/2008/05/caught-by-the-reaper-8/"
    "The Feather Bender: The Dog Nobbler (Barry Ord Clarke)" url="https://thefeatherbender.com/the-dog-nobbler/"
    "Troutflies UK: Dog Nobbler" url="https://www.troutflies.co.uk/trout-fishing-flies/Lure-streamer-trout-flies/dog-nobbler-fishing-flies"
}
// Photos for checking proportions while authoring (pnpm refcheck); never published.
references {
    "https://www.fish4flies.com/img/flies/Large/1612-1612_1.jpg" page="https://www.fish4flies.com/Lures/Nobblers-and-Leadheads/Palmered-Eyed-Dog-Nobbler-Black" license="All rights reserved; reference only" flip=#true note="The palmered variant, side view"
    "https://www.troutflies.co.uk/image/cache/wp/gj/%20ALL%20NEW%20PICS/BOX%205/Dog%20nobbler%20Black-550x550w.webp" page="https://www.troutflies.co.uk/trout-fishing-flies/Lure-streamer-trout-flies/dog-nobbler-fishing-flies" license="All rights reserved; reference only" flip=#true note="Side view"
}

// Assumption: a long-shank lure hook; the photos show a shank of about three gapes.
hook nymph-2xl size=10
thread black size="6/0"

materials {
    // Assumption: an SSG or AAA shot, a little under a gape across.
    head split-shot color=black mm=4 label="Split shot, painted black"
    tail marabou color=black
    flash krystal-flash count=4 label="Pearl flash"
    rib silver-wire
    body chenille color=black
}

steps {
    slide-bead head note="Squeeze it on with pliers and glue it; many paint a batch of heads first."
    attach-thread at=0.82
    wrap-thread to=0.0
    // Read from the photos: a little over a shank past the bend.
    tie-in tail length=3.2 angle=8 spread=40 note="A long, full plume."
    tie-in flash length=3.0 note="Two strands each side."
    tie-in rib
    tie-in body
    wrap-thread to=0.82
    wind body to=0.82 turns=14 note="Up to the shot."
    tie-off body
    wind rib to=0.82 turns=5
    tie-off rib
    whip-finish note="Behind the shot."
}
